                            <div class='relative w-auto s:mr-0 mr-2 mb-2 last:mr-0 s:mt-0 s:flex s:flex-col l-:mb-0 flex-1'>
                    <img width="2560" height="1369" src="https://www.quantamagazine.org/wp-content/uploads/2056/08/Atom-Eiffel-tower-cr-Thierry-Lahaye_CNRS-scaled.webp" class="mb-6 w-full s:mb-4" alt="Six images showing 3D arrays of trapped atoms glowing green, arranged into different shapes: a hyperboloid, a Möbius strip, a fullerene-like sphere, a cone, a torus, and an Eiffel Tower." decoding="async" srcset="https://www.quantamagazine.org/wp-content/uploads/2056/08/Atom-Eiffel-tower-cr-Thierry-Lahaye_CNRS-scaled.webp 2560w, https://www.quantamagazine.org/wp-content/uploads/2056/08/Atom-Eiffel-tower-cr-Thierry-Lahaye_CNRS-1720x920.webp 1720w, https://www.quantamagazine.org/wp-content/uploads/2056/08/Atom-Eiffel-tower-cr-Thierry-Lahaye_CNRS-520x278.webp 520w, https://www.quantamagazine.org/wp-content/uploads/2056/08/Atom-Eiffel-tower-cr-Thierry-Lahaye_CNRS-768x411.webp 768w, https://www.quantamagazine.org/wp-content/uploads/2056/08/Atom-Eiffel-tower-cr-Thierry-Lahaye_CNRS-1536x821.webp 1536w, https://www.quantamagazine.org/wp-content/uploads/2056/08/Atom-Eiffel-tower-cr-Thierry-Lahaye_CNRS-2048x1095.webp 2048w, https://www.quantamagazine.org/wp-content/uploads/2056/08/Atom-Eiffel-tower-cr-Thierry-Lahaye_CNRS-98x52.webp 98w" sizes="(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px" />                </div>
